    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διοπτ-ήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spy, scout,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.562
				</span></i>
			: in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάγγελοι καὶ διοπτῆρες,</span> the
				<i>optiones</i> and <i>tesserarii</i> of the Romans, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
